KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ noexcept\(false expression\): SUCCESS$
^\[handler\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
optThrowDecl (parse.cpp) records noexcept(true) and noexcept(false) only;
any other expression is skipped and marked #C_noexcept_unevaluated.  The
noexcept operator takes such a function as non-throwing (assertion 1
fails), and the exception lowering does not call std::terminate when an
exception leaves it (the handler is not reached).  The expression has to
be kept, and evaluated when the function type is formed or instantiated.
